			"notes": "### v1.1.0 Beta for 1.21.1\n\n- New Mana System, replacing Energy Cell.\n\t- Slick new Mana HUD, configurable to your hearts content.\n\t- Modifiable with attributes: max mana and mana regeneration speed.\n\t- All previous weapons now use mana instead of Energy Cell.\n\t- A weapon's mana cost can be seen in the tooltip of the item.\n\t- Mana HUD will be hidden by default when it is not needed.\n- Added Bee Gun.\n\t- Crafted with 5 honey combs.\n\t- Bee Gun is a weapon that shoots an army of bees that home targets.\n- Added Gem Staffs.\n \t- Crafted from runes, Gem Staffs are the classic mage weapon that shoots orbs. Runes can be found in (rare to common) ruined portals, trial chambers and bastion treasures.\n\t- From best to worst: Echo, Diamond, Emerald, Amethyst, Lapis, Redstone.\n- Added Wand of Sparking.\n\t- Spawns in the bonus chest as a starter weapon. Can also crafted with a stick and a Rune.\n\t- Throws a spark that has a chance to set the target on fire.\n- Added Fallen Stars.\n\t- At night falling stars have a slight chance to spawn on sky near the player. Moon phase has an effect on drop rates.\n\t- Fallen Stars will disappear if left under the daylight.\n\t- 5 of Fallen Stars can be crafted into Mana Crystal which will grant +1 Mana Star. (20 mana)\n\t- Added a config option to set fallen star damage when it lands on top of an entity. (DISABLED BY DEFAULT)\n- 2 new Color Zapinators.\n\t- Added Yellow Zapinator with a 50% chance to spawn a lightning bolt when a target has been hit.\n\t- Added White Zapinator with a 50% chance to apply levitation to the target.\n- Meteorite armor now needs the whole set and saves mana only for Orange Zapinator, Gray Zapinator and Space Gun.\n- Increased Black Zapinator's damage from 999 to 69420.\n- Improved stability of laser projectiles.\n- Improved item descriptions and general localization to be more detailed and clear.\n- Tons of bugfixes."
		}
